    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get the long term view, but isn't it kind of unfair to basically tell these communities they have to wait for some future network to be built while their current roads are falling apart? it feels like the 'gradual approach' is just a way to dismiss the immediate necessity of driving. why is the transit side seen as the 'correct' direction for policy while highway spending is treated like something we just have to tolerate until we can stop doing it?",
